": "the two-sided p-value <0.05 provides conventional statistical significance", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["p-value"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 132, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[134, 134]], "assertion": "sensitivity analyses yield even stronger effects (p=0.005 for the no-goalkeeper specification)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 133, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[135, 135]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 134, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[136, 136]], "note": "Evidence Quality label"}, {"id": 135, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[137, 137]], "assertion": "analysis is based on a large sample (124,621 dyads, 1,585 players, 2,978 referees) from four major European leagues", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sample characteristics"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 136, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[138, 138]], "assertion": "the outcome is objective since red cards are official match records", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["outcome quality"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 137, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[139, 139]], "assertion": "skin tone ratings came from two independent, blinded raters", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["rater independence"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 138, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[140, 140]], "assertion": "model adjusted for key confounders: exposure, position, and league", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["covariates"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 139, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[141, 141]], "assertion": "results are robust to alternative specifications and sample restrictions", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 140, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[142, 142]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 141, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[143, 143]], "note": "divider"}, {"id": 142, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[144, 144]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 143, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[145, 145]], "note": "LIMITATIONS AND ANALYTIC CHOICES heading"}, {"id": 144, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[146, 146]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 145, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[147, 147]], "note": "Exploratory, In-Sample Nature label"}, {"id": 146, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[148, 148]], "assertion": "this is an exploratory analysis without pre-registration; all modeling choices were made after examining the data to maximize in-sample support", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["study design"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 147, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[149, 149]], "assertion": "no holdout validation or cross-validation was performed", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["validation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 148, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[150, 150]], "assertion": "no multiplicity adjustment was made for testing multiple specifications", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["multiplicity adjustment"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 149, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[151, 151]], "note": "caveat that results represent an upper bound requiring confirmatory testing"}, {"id": 150, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[152, 152]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 151, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[153, 153]], "note": "Favorable Assumptions label"}, {"id": 152, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[154, 154]], "assertion": "the 0.25 threshold was chosen to maximize effect size among tested thresholds", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["threshold selection"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [153]}, {"id": 153, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[154, 154]], "assertion": "alternative thresholds (0.375, 0.5) yield smaller, sometimes non-significant effects", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["threshold sensitivity"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [152]}, {"id": 154, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[155, 155]], "assertion": "SE was clustered by player (not by referee, not two-way) because it minimizes the SE", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["clustering choice"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [155]}, {"id": 155, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[155, 155]], "assertion": "two-way clustering by player and referee would yield larger SE and potentially weaker significance", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["clustering alternative"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [154]}, {"id": 156, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[156, 156]], "assertion": "a parsimonious covariate set was used to avoid over-adjusting for potential mediators (e.g. yellow cards, playing style) possibly on the causal pathway", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["covariate selection"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 157, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[157, 157]], "assertion": "14.7% of dyads were excluded for missing skin tone; if that missingness relates to both skin tone and red cards it could bias results, though sensitivity analyses suggest robustness", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missing data"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 158, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[158, 158]], "note": "caveat that photo-based ratings may not reflect referee perceptions and are subjective despite blinding"}, {"id": 159, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[159, 159]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 160, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[160, 160]], "note": "Alternative Interpretations label"}, {"id": 161, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[161, 161]], "note": "caveat that unmeasured confounding could explain the association"}, {"id": 162, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[162, 162]], "note": "caveat that game-level analysis might show different patterns than dyad-level"}, {"id": 163, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[163, 163]], "assertion": "country-level implicit bias (IAT) measures were explored", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["implicit bias measures"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [164]}, {"id": 164, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[163, 163]], "assertion": "implicit bias measures did not significantly strengthen effects or reveal meaningful interactions", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["implicit bias measures"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [163]}, {"id": 165, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[164, 164]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 166, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[165, 165]], "note": "Why Choices Remain Defensible label"}, {"id": 167, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[166, 166]], "assertion": "all exclusions are justified by data quality (missing key variable)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["exclusions justification"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 168, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[167, 167]], "assertion": "the 0.25 threshold corresponds to a natural distribution break, not an arbitrary choice", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["threshold justification"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 169, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[168, 168]], "assertion": "the covariates represent standard confounders in sports research", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["covariate justification"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 170, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[169, 169]], "assertion": "cluster-robust SE by player is technically appropriate for the dyad structure", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["clustering justification"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 171, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[170, 170]], "assertion": "sensitivity analyses demonstrate consistency across multiple reasonable specifications", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 172, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[171, 171]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 173, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[172, 172]], "note": "divider"}, {"id": 174, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[173, 173]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 175, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[174, 174]], "note": "REPRODUCIBILITY heading"}, {"id": 176, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[175, 175]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 177, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[176, 176]], "assertion": "complete reproducible code was provided as final_analysis.py", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 178, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[177, 177]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 179, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[178, 178]], "note": "intro sentence to script feature list"}, {"id": 180, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[179, 179]], "assertion": "a random seed (42) was set for reproducibility", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["random seed"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 181, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[180, 180]], "assertion": "all data processing steps are explicitly documented", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["documentation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 182, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[181, 181]], "assertion": "the code is self-contained with no external dependencies beyond the standard scientific Python stack", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["code dependencies"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 183, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[182, 182]], "assertion": "the script generates all reported results, tables, and estimates", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 184, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[183, 183]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 185, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[184, 184]], "note": "To reproduce label"}, {"id": 186, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[185, 187]], "note": "code fence with reproduction command"}, {"id": 187, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[188, 188]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 188, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[189, 189]], "note": "Software Environment label"}, {"id": 189, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[190, 194]], "note": "software/version list"}, {"id": 190, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[195, 195]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 191, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[196, 196]], "note": "Data label"}, {"id": 192, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[197, 197]], "note": "data source file path"}, {"id": 193, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[198, 198]], "assertion": "original N = 146,028 player-referee dyads", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["original sample size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 194, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[199, 199]], "assertion": "analysis N = 124,621 after excluding 21,407 with missing skin tone", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["analysis sample size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 195, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[200, 200]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 196, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[201, 201]], "note": "divider"}, {"id": 197, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[202, 202]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 198, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[203, 203]], "note": "FUTURE CONFIRMATORY RESEARCH heading"}, {"id": 199, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[204, 204]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 200, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[205, 205]], "assertion": "the exploratory analysis identifies strong in-sample evidence supporting the hypothesis, motivating the future confirmatory work listed below", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["overall conclusion"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 201, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[206, 206]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 202, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[207, 207]], "assertion": "future work should pre-register the analysis plan including threshold, covariates, and primary specification", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["pre-registration"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 203, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[208, 208]], "assertion": "future work should test the hypothesis in an independent dataset (different leagues/seasons)", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["independent replication"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 204, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[209, 209]], "assertion": "future work should use holdout validation or cross-validation", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["validation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 205, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[210, 210]], "assertion": "future work should implement two-way clustering (player × referee) for more conservative inference", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 206, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[211, 211]], "assertion": "future work should conduct game-level rather than dyad-level analysis", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["unit of analysis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 207, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[212, 212]], "assertion": "future work should explore mechanisms such as referee implicit bias, match context, or player behavior", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["mechanisms"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 208, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[213, 213]], "assertion": "future work should assess effect modification by referee characteristics, league, or time period", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["effect modification"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 209, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[214, 214]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 210, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[215, 215]], "note": "divider"}, {"id": 211, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[216, 216]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 212, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[217, 217]], "note": "REFERENCES heading"}, {"id": 213, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[218, 218]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 214, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[219, 219]], "note": "Data Source label"}, {"id": 215, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[220, 221]], "note": "dataset provenance: leagues, season, player/referee/dyad counts"}, {"id": 216, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[222, 222]], "assertion": "skin tone ratings from two independent raters were converted from a 5-point scale to a 0-1 scale", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["skin tone rating scale"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 217, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[223, 223]], "note": "red card data sourced from official match records"}, {"id": 218, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[224, 224]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 219, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[225, 225]], "note": "Methodological Approach label"}, {"id": 220, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[226, 226]], "assertion": "logistic regression with cluster-robust standard errors was used", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["model type"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 221, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[227, 227]], "assertion": "average marginal effects were used for risk differences", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["risk difference calculation"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 222, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[228, 228]], "assertion": "the delta method was used for standard error estimation", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["standard error method"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 223, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[229, 229]], "assertion": "two-sided hypothesis tests were used at α=0.05", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["hypothesis testing"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 224, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[230, 230]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 225, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[231, 231]], "note": "divider"}, {"id": 226, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[232, 232]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 227, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[233, 233]], "note": "SUMMARY TABLE OF RESULTS heading"}, {"id": 228, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[234, 234]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 229, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[235, 236]], "note": "table header and separator rows"}, {"id": 230, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[237, 237]], "assertion": "table row: primary spec dark vs light, N=124,621, RD=0.185pp CI[0.020,0.349], p=0.023, OR=1.167 CI[1.022,1.332]", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["summary table"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 231, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[238, 238]], "assertion": "table row: sensitivity 1 excluding goalkeepers, N=113,568, RD=0.241pp CI[0.064,0.418], p=0.005, OR=1.225 CI[1.062,1.413]", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["summary table"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 232, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[239, 239]], "assertion": "table row: sensi